# .wolf/memory.md is an append-only session log: every session appends a block
# at the end, so two branches almost always "conflict" on the same tail even
# though neither touched the other's entries. The built-in union driver keeps
# both sides instead of stopping for a merge that has no real decision in it.
#
# Union applies only to hunks that actually conflict, so a one-sided deletion
# (the 7-day compression cron) is still resolved by the normal 3-way merge.
#
# Deliberately scoped to this one file. Union on the .wolf JSON state files
# would emit structurally invalid JSON, and on cerebrum.md/STATUS.md - which
# are edited in place rather than appended to - it would duplicate sections.
.wolf/memory.md merge=union
